    <backmatter>
      <appendix xml:id="glossary-guide">
        <title>Definitions, quantities, laws and models</title>
        <p>Scientific statements do different jobs. A definition fixes meaning; a quantity is measurable; a unit is an agreed standard; a model is a useful representation; an empirical law describes a regularity; a theory is an explanatory framework supported by evidence. The book labels these distinctions where they matter.</p>
      </appendix>
    </backmatter>
